## 5. Mandatory Platform Violation Rules

<div class="portal-alert-box">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">NON-NEGOTIABLE ARCHITECTURAL POLICIES</div>
  <p>Pull Requests violating any of these four constraints will be automatically rejected by Danger CI:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Zero Unapproved Frameworks:</strong> Flutter, Xamarin, Cordova, and Ionic are strictly forbidden. Applications must select from the 3 Tier-1 stacks.</li>
    <li><strong>Declarative UI Only:</strong> Legacy Android XML layouts and iOS UIKit Storyboards are deprecated. All new feature code must use Jetpack Compose, SwiftUI, or React Native.</li>
    <li><strong>Strict Type Safety:</strong> Untyped JavaScript or blanket <code>Any</code> (Kotlin) / <code>AnyObject</code> (Swift) type escapes are forbidden. All data boundaries must have strict contracts.</li>
    <li><strong>No Custom Core Re-inventions:</strong> Never write custom token stores, custom HTTP retry layers, or custom analytics pipelines. Use the approved <code>@enterprise/*</code>, SPM, and Maven internal SDKs.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

